.TH ROOT 1 "October 2026" "Root 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
root \- deterministic, local-first resource inspection utility for agentic workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B root
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Root
is a deterministic, local-first system resource inspection and monitoring utility designed to help developers audit, track, and safely observe resources accumulated through agentic coding workflows.
.PP
Root operates under strict least-privilege principles, requiring zero elevated privileges and executing no mutating or destructive filesystem actions in production.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Probe system capabilities, kernel interfaces, memory distribution, and XDG paths.
.TP
\fBstatus\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Display a concise overview of system telemetry, memory pressure, and activity.
.TP
\fBscan\fR \fB\-\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-interactive\fR]
Scan and audit development resources within the specified target directory.
.TP
\fBdiscover\fR [\fB\-\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-agents\fR] [\fB\-\-tools\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-tool\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Discover and classify footprints from AI coding agents and development tooling.
.TP
\fBinspect\fR \fImemory\fR|\fIprocesses\fR|\fIstorage\fR|\fItransactions\fR
Deep-dive into specific subsystem telemetry and accounting.
.TP
\fBexplain\fR \fIRESOURCE_ID\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Explain provenance, matched classification rules, and Guardian policy for a resource.
.TP
\fBreport\fR [\fB\-\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Generate comprehensive diagnostic audit report.
.TP
\fBmonitor\fR [\fB\-\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-processes\fR] [\fB\-\-budget-entries\fR \fIN\fR]
Start live, rate-limited, read-only filesystem and process observation.
.TP
\fBschedule\fR \fIstatus\fR|\fIenable\fR|\fIdisable\fR|\fIhistory\fR
Manage unprivileged user-level scheduled inspection timers.
.SH SAFETY INVARIANTS
Root v1.0 operates exclusively in Read-Only Safety Mode. All destructive commands (clean, delete, quarantine, restore, prune) are permanently rejected by the Guardian security engine in production.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, disables terminal color formatting.
